p cnf 11 10
c A depth-limited trap.cnf: same structure, 3 triples instead of 7, so a
c plain DPLL search finishes in a few thousand events instead of millions.

c --- THE TRAP ---
c These clauses are easily satisfied but create a
c tree of valid assignments for variables 1 through 9.
c Each triple admits 6 of its 8 assignments, so the search
c below it is entered 6^3 = 216 times.
1 2 3 0
-1 -2 -3 0
4 5 6 0
-4 -5 -6 0
7 8 9 0
-7 -8 -9 0

c --- THE CONTRADICTION ---
c Variables 10 and 11 form a standalone logical impossibility.
10 11 0
-10 11 0
10 -11 0
-10 -11 0
